The iPhone Duo's Quick Look feature appears to have a two-page layout option when the foldable is held in its open-book orientation, based on a new finding by code explorer pdfu.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/iphone-duo-feature.jpg" alt="" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1068262" /><br/>
A video clip <a href="https://x.com/itspdfu/status/2107467371141374296?s=20">shared on X</a> shows an Apple Style Guide document previewed across both halves of the unfolded iPhone, with consecutive pages displayed side by side like a spread. When navigating the document, the Quick Look interface displays search, markup, and share controls along the right-hand side.<br/>
<br/>
The layout would make Quick Look the latest feature to take advantage of the Duo's wide-format display. Apple has already detailed how iOS 27 <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/10/apple-details-how-ios-27-adapts-to-iphone-duo/">adapts interfaces</a> for the device, including angle-aware layouts and side-by-side multitasking.<br/>
